---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ActorLab from "../components/ActorLab.astro";
import Playground from "../components/Playground.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Identity playground — Janitor"
  description="Explore Janitor’s real browser matching and delegation checks with synthetic scenarios. Nothing is collected or sent."
>
  <main id="main" class="container standalone-lab">
    <div class="page-breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Janitor</a>
      <span>/</span>Playground
    </div>
    <h1>Try Janitor in your browser</h1>
    <p class="playground-intro">
      Explore how a visitor ID survives browser changes, then see how people and
      agents share an account. Both examples use made-up data and run entirely
      on this page.
    </p>
    <Playground />
    <ActorLab />
    <div class="experiment-note">
      <h2>What this demo shows</h2>
      <p>
        The labs run <code>@janitor/core</code> in your browser against made-up
        browser history and example login records. It does not use a real
        cookie, collect browser signals, call Jev, or send observations to a
        server. The same matching and delegation logic powers the library.
      </p>
      <p>
        The example shows scores so you can see how matching works. Production
        HTTP responses keep scores private by default. Identity confidence is an
        experimental matching score. It is not authentication or proof that two
        people are the same person.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/validation/">
        Testing and limitations ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
